OWNER-CURRENT READOUT
  owner_current treats theorem exits as signed boundary currents:
    unit-petal-named rows are unit-boundary inflows;
    positive-Haar-open rows are covering-floor outflows.
  theorem target: the first endpoint-owner leak in an enlarged HYP-2963
  bank must become a Farkas/Green dual certificate, AP/GW boundary H1,
  forbidden H7 lift, or named residual owner-current debt.

TROPICAL-WALL READOUT
  v2_word alone repeats the HYP-3311 warning:
    drop6 fattening core add180 and petal 10->20 share the same v2 word
    but have different theorem exits.
  tropical_wall adds the first bending owner / wall type and separates
  that collision without using the full residue word.
  theorem target: same-residue or same-v2 height flex must cross a
  Newton/secondary-fan wall with positive off-grid floor, land on the
  AP/GW 12->24 hinge, or emit height-discriminant debt.

